From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:10:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/44] qwen27: dump each vision block's residual for a parity
 curve

TF_QWEN_VISION_BLOCKS copies a block's residual aside as it finishes, one buffer a
block, allocated only when the flag is set so an unset run costs nothing. A small
qwv_copy_bf16 kernel turns the tower's fp32 residual into the bf16 rows a
reference comparison wants.

Measured on this checkpoint, chart at 16x36 patches, all 27 blocks plus the
merger against transformers in bf16: engine rms tracks the reference within 0.2%
at every block, cos never below 0.9989, and there is no step. Block 26's absolute
error jumps to 4864 only because the tower's own activations jump there (reference
rms 1.5 -> 186), and the engine follows that jump.

The engine is also closer to an fp32 reference than bf16 is: engine vs fp32 max
1.64 cos 0.99952, while HF bf16 vs HF fp32 is max 3.86 cos 0.99784. So the tower
sits at the model's own noise floor, not above it.
---
 zig/kernels/metal/core/qwen_vision.metal |  8 +++++
 zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig           | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 zig/src/native/qwen27_images.zig         |  8 +++++
 zig/src/platform/environment.zig         |  1 +
 4 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zig/kernels/metal/core/qwen_vision.metal b/zig/kernels/metal/core/qwen_vision.metal
index 69e80ecd7..65c97553f 100644
--- a/zig/kernels/metal/core/qwen_vision.metal
+++ b/zig/kernels/metal/core/qwen_vision.metal
@@ -147,3 +147,11 @@ struct QwvAct {
   const ulong i = ulong(at.y) * width + at.x;
   y[i] = bfloat(float(y[i]) + float(b[at.x]));
 }
+
+// A parity dump's copy: the tower's fp32 residual to bf16 rows, for comparison with a reference.
+[[max_total_threads_per_threadgroup(256)]] [[kernel]] void qwv_copy_bf16(
+    const device float* x [[buffer(0)]], device bfloat* y [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& cells [[buffer(2)]],
+    uint at [[thread_position_in_grid]]) {
+  if (at >= cells) return;
+  y[at] = bfloat(x[at]);
+}
diff --git a/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig b/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig
index 2d597689b..13d9944b9 100644
--- a/zig/src/core/qwen_vl/tower.zig
